/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 44 0 R
/T (In a conventional parking system, security personnel may have to manually count vehicles and check whether parking spaces are available. This can result in errors, delays, and inefficient use of parking space. A digital automatic parking system can solve these problems by continuously monitoring vehicle entry and exit.)
/E (In a conventional parking system, security personnel may have to manually count vehicles and check whether parking spaces are available. This can result in errors, delays, and inefficient use of parking space. A digital automatic parking system can solve these problems by continuously monitoring vehicle entry and exit.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
